<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer gets cancer drug okays.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer gets cancer drug okays.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said  Thursday that it has received regulatory authorization to market Campto,  a new anticancer agent, in Belgium, Bulgaria, India, Israel, Italy,  Tunisia and Ukraine.</p>
<p>Campto is indicated for the treatment of advanced metastatic colorectal  cancer that has failed to respond to standard chemotherapy with 5-fluorouracil  (5-FU).</p>
<p>The drug has now been approved in 20 countries and is available in  eight.</p>
<p>According to Rhone-Poulenc, Campto is the first therapeutic innovation  in colorectal cancer in nearly 40 years and is the first in a new  class of agents that act by inhibiting topoisomerase-I, a key enzyme  necessary for cancer cell growth.</p>
</text>
